				"avatarUrl": "https://fediverse.zachleat.com/avatars/original/missing.png"
			},
			"date": "2023-08-22T11:12:27.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> I can confidently report that working for a VC -funded startup is almost always going to end in tears for the employees.</p><p>It was a Friday. The 23 FTEs who were fired that morning went on to other work, often unrelated to their jobs at the startup (for the love of the gods, don’t work for a VC startup as a career ladder step. I don’t even know where to start on that idea), but the leaders of the company have vanished into obscurity.</p>",
