			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://defcon.social/@corbin\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>corbin</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://fosstodon.org/@boneskull\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>boneskull</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> text to text is pretty lossy and interpreted code always on a back foot wrt optimization so wasm def seems inevitable.</p><p>But I've been saying this for a decade at least now too. I have no issue with the techniques but question their assumed universal application.</p>",
